# A11 / Gate 1 — FROZEN CROSS-SERVICE CONTRACTS.
#
# These files are pinned by SHA-256 in `certification/a11/A11_SNAPSHOT.sha256`,
# so their BYTES are load-bearing, not just their content. Without a rule here
# `core.autocrlf` decides: git stores LF, checks out LF on Linux and CRLF on
# Windows, and the same commit therefore hashes to two different digests
# depending on who cloned it. The certification reproducer then reports
# "the certified bytes moved" on one platform and not the other — drift that
# is really a checkout setting, which is the single most misleading failure a
# certification tool can produce.
#
# Pin to LF so one commit means one digest everywhere.
*.json    text eol=lf
